--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
does not uniquely resolve
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5: when a function template's requires-clause was
checked, a trailing type parameter PACK was mapped to its FIRST deduced
element only, so libstdc++'s `__adaptor_partial_app_viable<_Take, int(&)[5],
int>` (`sizeof...(_Args) == _S_arity - 1`) came out true for two arguments and
_RangeAdaptor's partial-application operator() stayed viable against _Take's
own two-argument one ("does not uniquely resolve", then `views::take(3)`
built the wrong closure).  Non-vacuous: the last assertion states a wrong
value and must FAIL.
